+  # compiles a `#![no_std] #![no_main]` program instead — because a
+  # freestanding target has no libstd to link. Reading the same property
+  # here keeps Mesa and Meson agreeing about the same machine rather
+  # than each deciding separately.
+  #
+  # Where it is false, Mesa's Rust crates are built #![no_std] against
+  # `core` and `alloc`, and exactly one Rust staticlib may exist in the
+  # binary — see src/nouveau/rust_runtime/lib.rs for why.
+  with_rust_std = host_machine.kernel() != 'none'
